/*!
\page page_stFpsSlat StFpsSlat

\brief Single scintillator slat in the FPS (FPD Pre-Shower) preshower detector.

\section fpsSlat_overview Overview

StFpsSlat stores the MIP signal and associated FMS photon points for one
scintillator slat in the FPS (Forward Pion Spectrometer) pre-shower detector,
which sits directly in front of the FMS lead-glass calorimeter (2.5 < η < 4.0).

The FPS has four quadrants, three scintillator layers each, and 21 slats per
layer, giving 252 slats total (\c kFpsMaxSlat=252).  Slat IDs encode quadrant,
layer, and slat number within the layer:

\code
slatId = (quad-1)*63 + (layer-1)*21 + (slat-1)
\endcode

Each FMS photon point is projected onto the FPS; matching slat MIP signals
are used to classify photon/electron/hadron via the FPS PID flag in
\ref page_stFmsPoint "StFmsPoint".

All data members are transient (not persistified).

\section fpsSlat_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StFpsSlat
\endcode

Stored in \ref page_stFmsCollection "StFmsCollection" as a transient vector.

\section fpsSlat_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Int_t | mSlatId | FPS slat ID [0, 251] (transient). |
| Float_t | mMip | MIP signal in this slat (transient). |
| UInt_t[5] | mNPoint | Associated point counts by proximity rank: [0]=closest, [4]=total (transient). |
| StPtrVecFmsPoint | mPoint1..4 | FMS photon points at proximity ranks 0–3 (transient). |

\section fpsSlat_methods Key Methods

- \c slatId() — slat ID.
- \c mip() — MIP signal.
- \c nPoint(int type) — count of associated FMS points at proximity rank type.
- \c point(int type) — vector of FMS points at proximity rank type.
- \c addPoint(StFmsPoint*, int type) — associate an FMS point.
- \c setSlatId(), \c setMip() — setters.
- \c print() — print summary.

\section fpsSlat_seealso See Also

\ref page_stFmsPoint "StFmsPoint",
\ref page_stFmsPointPair "StFmsPointPair",
\ref page_stFmsCluster "StFmsCluster"
*/
